caption: Capture sidebar hooks
title: Capture sidebar hooks
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Summary
Add an entry to the capture sidebar: a "new (thing)" button, a defaults control (a labelled line such as //Default context://), or any other line.

! Detail
The capture sidebar renders its entries — the members of `$:/tags/hypergsd/Capture` — grouped into numbered portions, one line per member; a member's `Portion/<n>` tag names its portion (numbers only; an untagged member lands in Portion/1). The shipped portions:

;Portion/1
:Capture defaults — the shipped members are the //Default realm:// picker (core) and the //Default context:// select, each member owning both its label and its control.
;Portion/2
:The common new-item buttons: new action, new project, new reference.
;Portion/3
:The rarer new-item buttons: new contact, new context.
;Portion/4
:The realm note.

A button is usually a single `<$hgsd.new-button>` invocation with its own `lingo-base` (tooltip/aria via full-path transclusions in attribute position). The button for a type shipped by a sub-plugin must live in that sub-plugin: absence of the plugin removes the member (and its strings) structurally, with no existence gate needed. A portion whose members are all absent renders no gap.

Within-portion order is the engine's tag-list order — the tag list's `list` field first, then member `list-before`/`list-after` pins (the new-reference button pins itself after the core new-project button), then engine order; a user-level `list` field (written by the drag list below) overrides the pins. Order and visibility are configured in Settings → Sidebar: one drag list for the whole tab, a numeric Portion picker on every row (pick a number in use, or the next-free number it offers to start a fresh portion), and the checkbox hides an entry — `$:/config/hypergsd/Capture/visibility/<title>`, default show. The review sidebar works the same way over `$:/tags/hypergsd/Review`.

! Best Practice
Give a new-item button a `gsd-type` matching a `$:/tags/hypergsd/Type` tag-list member, and inherit the defaults by passing no `gsd-project`/`gsd-realm` — the capture sidebar's effective context/realm flow through `$hgsd.new-button`'s inheritance. Pick the portion that matches how common the item is, or claim any free number of your own.
